  "text": "## What is the difference between custom software and off-the-shelf software?\n\nCustom software is engineered specifically to match an organization's unique business processes, eliminating vendor fees and rigid limitations. Off-the-shelf software is pre-packaged for general markets, often requiring businesses to change their workflows to fit the tool.",
